arguments.command:
cd /workspace/target && cat <<'EOF' > investigation.json
{
  "candidate_hash": "df6596664871a87b0994d833e540e9fab603029cab76c26a4af7b5024955ae71",
  "code_hash": "6d8f6ccdf6e740f43622ecc61516d938f5c7273423a4b4c12c3d304eb48b8c31",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "id": "ev-3a8da0c504614e8d",
      "observation": "Four exports use mixed delimiters (comma, semicolon, pipe, comma); two need column renames, one needs 0.01 weather rescaling from percent to 0-1, and the March-April export has 1533 raw rows that must deduplicate on instant to 1461 unique rows. The current loader skips both the scale_to_canonical rules and deduplication, so profile.current shows 11611 rows instead of 11539 and weather_max of 100.0 instead of 1.0."
    },
    {
      "id": "ev-81d7a438fa332d0f",
      "observation": "Requests contain only the 14 issue-time columns; casual, registered, and cnt are outcomes present solely in labeled history and must never enter the feature matrix. The starter FEATURES list is compliant but the loader and model must stay compliant while the pipeline is strengthened."
    },
    {
      "id": "ev-9a13f0f698055a15",
      "observation": "Paired month demand shows year-over-year growth: Jan 130.6/55.5=2.35x, Feb 149.0/74.3=2.01x, Mar 221.9/87.7=2.53x, Apr 242.7/131.9=1.84x. The terminal months 9-12 exist in history only for year 0, so a tree fit with a raw yr feature cannot extrapolate the year-1 level into September-December; an explicit multiplicative year bridge estimated from overlapping months is required."
    },
    {
      "id": "ev-359426edf27b87b9",
      "observation": "Working-day commute hours 7-9 and 16-18 have sharply elevated means (e.g., hr 17 year 1 mean 529.4 vs year 0 mean 394.9). A mean-only DummyRegressor cannot represent the hour-by-workingday interaction, so commute-hour MAE will fail; the model needs hour granularity interacted with workingday, e.g. a gradient boosted tree over hour, workingday and weather plus an explicit commute indicator."
    },
    {
      "id": "ev-39620aa8e8b89e15",
      "observation": "The terminal horizon is 2,888 rows spanning 2012-09-01 through 2012-12-31, four months beyond the visible 2012-04-30 history end, with same-hour weather available at issue time. Runtime validation advances history through August 2012, so the pipeline must adapt to whatever history end it is served and bridge the remaining gap with the year growth factor while calibrating intervals on a forward chronological holdout."
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "The release fails for three compounding reasons. First, the loader ignores the registry scale_to_canonical and deduplicate_on rules, so 2012 Jan-Feb weather enters at a 0-100 scale while all other exports are 0-1 and 72 duplicate March-April rows are double counted, corrupting both training and any growth estimate. Second, the model is a global-mean DummyRegressor, which cannot represent hour-of-day, workingday commute peaks, weather response, or the roughly 1.8x-2.5x year-over-year demand growth, so the September-December year-1 horizon is systematically underpredicted. Third, interval_radius takes the 0.20 quantile of absolute forward residuals instead of the 0.80 quantile, producing intervals far too narrow to reach 70 percent coverage. Normalizing the exports per the registry, training a gradient boosted tree on issue-time features with the year-1 target detrended by a month-weighted growth factor estimated from overlapping calendar months (then re-inflating predictions for year-1 requests), and calibrating a symmetric 80 percent radius from the 0.80 quantile of forward chronological holdout residuals will bring overall RMSE under 65, month RMSE under 72, commute MAE under 76, coverage into 70-98 percent, and mean width under 250.",
  "planned_test": "After the commitment: rerun scripts/run_backtest.py to confirm 11539 unique rows, weather_max 1.0, and fold RMSE far below the dummy 210-232 baseline; run the visible unittest suite to confirm the feature matrix still excludes outcomes; run a local forward replay that trains on history through 2012-04-30 with the growth bridge and checks chronological holdout RMSE, commute-hour MAE, interval coverage near 80 percent, and mean width under 250; verify scripts/predict.py output is deterministic across seeds and invariant to independent history and request row permutations; then drive the full ordered service walk through validate, recovery, the second deployment, audits, canary, production, freeze, and submit."
}
EOF
python3 -c "import json;d=json.load(open('investigation.json'));print('ok', d['candidate_hash'][:8], len(d['evidence']))"

